More teams than run at once on the machine's GPU (docs/INPROGRESS.md,
Processes as teams, step 4): a region without team mailboxes runs its 2000
teams a few at a time; a region with them ends the program once no more of
its teams have started for the stall time, saying how many ran at once. The
default is ten seconds, so that a region on a GPU that other programs fill
waits for them; this one is known to have too many, so it sets a second
(MERK_TEAMS_STALL_MILLISECONDS), not to hold the GPU from the tests beside
it for longer, whose teams would not start meanwhile.
REQUIRES: amdgpu-gpu

RUN: merkc -O2 -fopenmp --offload-arch=%offload-arch %libomp-flags %S/Inputs/omp-target-teams-too-many.m -o %t
RUN: %libomp-env OMP_TARGET_OFFLOAD=MANDATORY MERK_TEAMS_STALL_MILLISECONDS=1000 not %t > %t.out 2> %t.err
RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=OUTPUT --match-full-lines --strict-whitespace < %t.out
RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ERROR --match-full-lines --strict-whitespace < %t.err

OUTPUT:teams without team mailboxes: 2000
OUTPUT-NOT:{{.}}
ERROR:Mercury runtime: target teams: only {{[1-9][0-9]*}} of the 2000 teams ran at once on the device, and the teams of a region with team mailboxes must all run at once
ERROR-NOT:{{.}}

A stall time that is not a positive number is an error at start-up.
RUN: %libomp-env MERK_TEAMS_STALL_MILLISECONDS=soon not %t 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=BAD
BAD:Mercury runtime: MERK_TEAMS_STALL_MILLISECONDS is not a positive number of milliseconds: soon
